      'The Topic 5 lectures on the Class 10, 11 and 13 pages are Canvas Studio embeds that are not mirrored here. Only the 2-to-1 MUX recap is mirrored, and the “equations and circuits” video it points to is missing too. So the 2-to-1 MUX equation, 4-to-1 and 8-to-1 MUXes, MUX trees, MUX-based function generation, decoders (enable, active-low outputs, building larger decoders, implementing functions) and the DEMUX are supplemental textbook material. The few course facts used for them come from the one-line decoder recap in Class 12 Video 1 and from Topic 6 videos that use 2-to-1 and 4-to-1 MUXes.',
      'No mirrored lecture covers the ALU or carry-lookahead adders. Both are on the hub’s Final Exam page, so they are covered here as supplemental textbook material. The ALU op-code table is the app’s own; check the op codes your exam uses.',
      'Two Topic 5 videos are partial uploads. Class 13 Video 1 stops at 03:44, before the top-down steps after the K-map. Class 16 Video 2 stops at 01:06, as the 4-bit comparator design begins. The 4-bit cascade wiring and the MSB stage’s inputs (EQin = 1, GTin = LTin = 0) are derived here from the 1-bit comparator equations in Class 16 Video 3.',
